  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAs">VI As</ref> 1.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-q">Et qui cum fure stabit et conpugnabit, cum fure deponatur.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-h">⁊ se ðe mid þeofe stánde ⁊ midfeohte, lecge hine man mid þam þeofe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="[1].3" corresp="#wit-h">⁊ se ðe mid þeofe stánde ⁊ midfeohte, lecge hine man mid þam þeofe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">And he who stands by a thief and fights on his side, shall be slain with the thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wer zu einem Diebe steht und [ihm] zur Seite ficht: ihn schlage man mitsammt dem Diebe nieder.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever stands with a thief and fights alongside [him]: let him be struck down together with the thief.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II As 1.5.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
